 "result": "They're werkzeug `LocalProxy` objects backed by a single `ContextVar`.\n\n- **`src/tessel/globals.py`**: defines `_app_var = ContextVar(\"tessel.app_ctx\")`, which holds the current `AppContext`. Each proxy is a `werkzeug.local.LocalProxy` over that var:\n  - `active_app` → the context's `.app` attribute (the `Tessel` instance)\n  - `g` → `.g` (the `_AppCtxGlobals` object)\n  - `request` → `.request` (the `Request`)\n  - `session` → `.session`\n  - `app_ctx` → the `AppContext` itself\n- **`src/tessel/ctx.py`**: `AppContext` holds `app`, `g`, `request` and `session`. Its push/pop sets and resets `_app_var`, which is what `with app.app_context()` and the request cycle in `src/tessel/app.py` do.\n\nOn each attribute access, the proxy reads the context var for the current thread or async task and then looks up the named attribute on that `AppContext`. If no context is set, it raises the \"outside of application/request context\" error.\n\n`request_ctx` is now a deprecated alias for `app_ctx`. Request and app contexts have been merged into one.",
